[{:db/id 17592186064311 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5c789989-28b9-52e0-ac72-a0f8b7d66a60"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5c789989-28b9-52e0-ac72-a0f8b7d66a60" :question/id #uuid "5c789989-28b9-52e0-ac72-a0f8b7d66a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-138860" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}.$ The derivative of this function is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)(11{x}^{2}+24x-2)}{g(x)}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Our function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}}{\\sqrt[3]{3x+6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6/3}}{(3x+6)^{1/3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{2}}{(3x+6)^{1/3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{2}}{(3x+6)^{1/3}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({x}^{2}+2)^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((3x+6)^{1/3}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x+6)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3x+6}\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+2}-\\frac{1}{3x+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+2}-\\frac{1}{3x+6})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}(\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+2}-\\frac{1}{3x+6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}(\\frac{4x(3x+6)-({x}^{2}+2)}{({x}^{2}+2)(3x+6)}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}(\\frac{11{x}^{2}+24x-2}{({x}^{2}+2)(3x+6)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)(11{x}^{2}+24x-2)}{\\sqrt[3]{(3x-6)^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\sqrt[3]{(3x-6)^{4}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c497ffd-4cca-50b5-a7fc-dc93d720ea25"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c497ffd-4cca-50b5-a7fc-dc93d720ea25" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c497ffd-4cca-50b5-a7fc-dc93d720ea25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c88b7035-072c-5214-bd55-1804a6aa0ae7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec4a59e0-949a-5cc8-91d2-09ecb393925e" "answer-80386a1f-1c68-542d-97ab-e6ec02fe80f1" "answer-9eb339eb-1cc4-5d35-9e83-6c06760cd1fe" "answer-c88b7035-072c-5214-bd55-1804a6aa0ae7" "answer-e2ae8cb1-1ad1-519a-a9ae-fc0f9b33b01f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec4a59e0-949a-5cc8-91d2-09ecb393925e" :answer/id #uuid "ec4a59e0-949a-5cc8-91d2-09ecb393925e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{(x+2)^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80386a1f-1c68-542d-97ab-e6ec02fe80f1" :answer/id #uuid "80386a1f-1c68-542d-97ab-e6ec02fe80f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sqrt[3]{(x+2)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9eb339eb-1cc4-5d35-9e83-6c06760cd1fe" :answer/id #uuid "9eb339eb-1cc4-5d35-9e83-6c06760cd1fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{(3x+6)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c88b7035-072c-5214-bd55-1804a6aa0ae7" :answer/id #uuid "c88b7035-072c-5214-bd55-1804a6aa0ae7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{(3x+6)^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2ae8cb1-1ad1-519a-a9ae-fc0f9b33b01f" :answer/id #uuid "e2ae8cb1-1ad1-519a-a9ae-fc0f9b33b01f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{3x+6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-93bbf55d-a1b3-5160-aa13-5dae73451322" :activity/id #uuid "93bbf55d-a1b3-5160-aa13-5dae73451322" :activity/title "Further Logarithmic Differentiation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048919 :activity/course 17592186046645 :activity/steps ["step-85cfab1f-9554-509a-b407-c56fc29d97eb" "step-96a56253-16ed-52e2-abe6-273309cfe7a7" "step-2ba10ec7-4252-52ba-8bc0-ceb77d7dadf1" "step-73bd8f64-f826-5721-8dca-5f9a8f22b62d" "step-d420e20c-8165-5de9-8370-feb30c2da60d"] :activity/first-step "step-85cfab1f-9554-509a-b407-c56fc29d97eb" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-85cfab1f-9554-509a-b407-c56fc29d97eb" :step/id #uuid "85cfab1f-9554-509a-b407-c56fc29d97eb" :step/content 17592186534079 :step/next "step-96a56253-16ed-52e2-abe6-273309cfe7a7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-96a56253-16ed-52e2-abe6-273309cfe7a7" :step/id #uuid "96a56253-16ed-52e2-abe6-273309cfe7a7" :step/content 17592186534090 :step/next "step-2ba10ec7-4252-52ba-8bc0-ceb77d7dadf1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2ba10ec7-4252-52ba-8bc0-ceb77d7dadf1" :step/id #uuid "2ba10ec7-4252-52ba-8bc0-ceb77d7dadf1" :step/content 17592186534067 :step/next "step-73bd8f64-f826-5721-8dca-5f9a8f22b62d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-73bd8f64-f826-5721-8dca-5f9a8f22b62d" :step/id #uuid "73bd8f64-f826-5721-8dca-5f9a8f22b62d" :step/content "question-5c789989-28b9-52e0-ac72-a0f8b7d66a60" :step/next "step-d420e20c-8165-5de9-8370-feb30c2da60d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d420e20c-8165-5de9-8370-feb30c2da60d" :step/id #uuid "d420e20c-8165-5de9-8370-feb30c2da60d" :step/content 17592186534031 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166962 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5964ffcf-bc61-5cdb-8ce3-fe3d629e8c05"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5964ffcf-bc61-5cdb-8ce3-fe3d629e8c05" :question/id #uuid "5964ffcf-bc61-5cdb-8ce3-fe3d629e8c05" :question/math-academy-id "q-340513" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $f(x)$ is the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F(x)$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x+2\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\nII. $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\nIII. $f(x+\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f$ is the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F,$ we have \n\n- $f(x+2\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,2\\pi ).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. This is exactly the definition of $2\\pi $-periodicity:\n\n$$\nf(x+2\\pi )=f(x)\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that $F$ itself is $2\\pi $-periodic, because for any $x\\in R,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x+2\\pi )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+2\\pi )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)=F(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $F$ already satisfies the periodicity rule, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension agrees with $F$ everywhere, so $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, take $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi )=f(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=F(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5932e5d0-9d0c-54be-9a78-8ee0938071e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5932e5d0-9d0c-54be-9a78-8ee0938071e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "5932e5d0-9d0c-54be-9a78-8ee0938071e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a7281cf1-df65-5001-bdd3-ab6876280750" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a7281cf1-df65-5001-bdd3-ab6876280750" "answer-e264fdd1-c875-5ee0-914c-54600fb544c3" "answer-c4208108-7b91-5e37-9f02-765baf72fbe9" "answer-bd204788-03a2-5b3d-ac8e-82ebffa05caf" "answer-7703407d-8788-52d9-8d23-7c0dd469068b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7281cf1-df65-5001-bdd3-ab6876280750" :answer/id #uuid "a7281cf1-df65-5001-bdd3-ab6876280750" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e264fdd1-c875-5ee0-914c-54600fb544c3" :answer/id #uuid "e264fdd1-c875-5ee0-914c-54600fb544c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4208108-7b91-5e37-9f02-765baf72fbe9" :answer/id #uuid "c4208108-7b91-5e37-9f02-765baf72fbe9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd204788-03a2-5b3d-ac8e-82ebffa05caf" :answer/id #uuid "bd204788-03a2-5b3d-ac8e-82ebffa05caf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7703407d-8788-52d9-8d23-7c0dd469068b" :answer/id #uuid "7703407d-8788-52d9-8d23-7c0dd469068b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068927 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aa2d0b41-12c5-5cc7-a265-9b2befe09045" "question-e629f775-4d70-5fe8-b2f0-8f18384b864c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa2d0b41-12c5-5cc7-a265-9b2befe09045" :question/id #uuid "aa2d0b41-12c5-5cc7-a265-9b2befe09045" :question/math-academy-id "q-31605" :question/problem "A horizontal line $l$ passes through the point $(5,4).$ Calculate the coordinates of the $y$-intercept of $l.$" :question/worked-solution "On any horizontal line, all points have the same $y$-coordinate.\n\nThe $y$-coordinate of the point $(5,4)$ is $4,$ so the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept is also $4.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-15c11955-b9c8-5da1-a467-21fb40fdcf4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-15c11955-b9c8-5da1-a467-21fb40fdcf4d" :answer-field/id #uuid "15c11955-b9c8-5da1-a467-21fb40fdcf4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a7ae48a6-8e60-521c-ae3d-ed5a35430fa0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a7ae48a6-8e60-521c-ae3d-ed5a35430fa0" "answer-fb242ae4-7619-5609-9b5f-113d3833b245" "answer-6fe93805-e84e-5076-bf14-f2778b50b1b3" "answer-5b155884-63bf-5f91-b031-664e4e3e1a13" "answer-89e9239d-84c4-5c3b-8534-6d11bbbf7dca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7ae48a6-8e60-521c-ae3d-ed5a35430fa0" :answer/id #uuid "a7ae48a6-8e60-521c-ae3d-ed5a35430fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb242ae4-7619-5609-9b5f-113d3833b245" :answer/id #uuid "fb242ae4-7619-5609-9b5f-113d3833b245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fe93805-e84e-5076-bf14-f2778b50b1b3" :answer/id #uuid "6fe93805-e84e-5076-bf14-f2778b50b1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b155884-63bf-5f91-b031-664e4e3e1a13" :answer/id #uuid "5b155884-63bf-5f91-b031-664e4e3e1a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89e9239d-84c4-5c3b-8534-6d11bbbf7dca" :answer/id #uuid "89e9239d-84c4-5c3b-8534-6d11bbbf7dca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no $y$-intercept" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e629f775-4d70-5fe8-b2f0-8f18384b864c" :question/id #uuid "e629f775-4d70-5fe8-b2f0-8f18384b864c" :question/math-academy-id "q-171725" :question/problem "A horizontal line $l$ passes through the point $(-3,2).$ What are the coordinates of the $y$-intercept of $l?$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept of $l$ are\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "On any horizontal line, all points have the same $y$-coordinate.\n\nThe $y$-coordinate of the point $(-3,2)$ is $2,$ so the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept is also $2.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-63e4ab55-d0a1-5786-9cc7-b2293a0bf11d" "answer-field-80d521d4-3885-53d4-af2a-71f3adfd567c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-63e4ab55-d0a1-5786-9cc7-b2293a0bf11d" :answer-field/id #uuid "63e4ab55-d0a1-5786-9cc7-b2293a0bf11d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-18fc2bc0-bf6d-5c95-b25a-160e38ec578c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18fc2bc0-bf6d-5c95-b25a-160e38ec578c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18fc2bc0-bf6d-5c95-b25a-160e38ec578c" :answer/id #uuid "18fc2bc0-bf6d-5c95-b25a-160e38ec578c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80d521d4-3885-53d4-af2a-71f3adfd567c" :answer-field/id #uuid "80d521d4-3885-53d4-af2a-71f3adfd567c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-972b3e5e-b37b-5a4f-991f-145fed1af8e3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-972b3e5e-b37b-5a4f-991f-145fed1af8e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-972b3e5e-b37b-5a4f-991f-145fed1af8e3" :answer/id #uuid "972b3e5e-b37b-5a4f-991f-145fed1af8e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2546e8f7-eee4-51d1-b227-0107b1dc1dff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2546e8f7-eee4-51d1-b227-0107b1dc1dff" :question/id #uuid "2546e8f7-eee4-51d1-b227-0107b1dc1dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-175915" :question/problem "The equation of the line that passes through the points $(2,8)$ and $(4,4)$ is $\\,y=${{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-8}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-2$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=-2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+b \\\\ 4 & =-2(4)+b \\\\ 4 & =-8+b \\\\ 4+8 & =b \\\\ 12 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the equation of the line is $y=-2\\,x+12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c136b416-aa9d-59c9-87d0-e2fd3b968a46" "answer-field-1f8264ee-8699-5a8d-b7d1-b9e37462db15"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c136b416-aa9d-59c9-87d0-e2fd3b968a46" :answer-field/id #uuid "c136b416-aa9d-59c9-87d0-e2fd3b968a46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-166db386-af1b-59c2-a6a5-51f8af225a25" :answer-field/choices ["answer-166db386-af1b-59c2-a6a5-51f8af225a25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-166db386-af1b-59c2-a6a5-51f8af225a25" :answer/id #uuid "166db386-af1b-59c2-a6a5-51f8af225a25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1f8264ee-8699-5a8d-b7d1-b9e37462db15" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f8264ee-8699-5a8d-b7d1-b9e37462db15" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ba7df070-8dc6-516c-b876-bba86140442c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba7df070-8dc6-516c-b876-bba86140442c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba7df070-8dc6-516c-b876-bba86140442c" :answer/id #uuid "ba7df070-8dc6-516c-b876-bba86140442c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c327bea7-f4fd-595a-8810-8984b4d4dea4" :activity/id #uuid "c327bea7-f4fd-595a-8810-8984b4d4dea4" :activity/title "Properties of Lines Given in Slope-Intercept Form" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049394 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-fa72bb9a-82e6-556f-a25d-dca4c2f9aee6" "step-c527ad9d-45ff-5250-97c1-54d0f5d7abf9" "step-80da2ac9-41e1-52d3-9494-12a39d637e6f"] :activity/first-step "step-fa72bb9a-82e6-556f-a25d-dca4c2f9aee6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fa72bb9a-82e6-556f-a25d-dca4c2f9aee6" :step/id #uuid "fa72bb9a-82e6-556f-a25d-dca4c2f9aee6" :step/content "question-aa2d0b41-12c5-5cc7-a265-9b2befe09045" :step/next "step-c527ad9d-45ff-5250-97c1-54d0f5d7abf9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c527ad9d-45ff-5250-97c1-54d0f5d7abf9" :step/id #uuid "c527ad9d-45ff-5250-97c1-54d0f5d7abf9" :step/content "question-e629f775-4d70-5fe8-b2f0-8f18384b864c" :step/next "step-80da2ac9-41e1-52d3-9494-12a39d637e6f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-80da2ac9-41e1-52d3-9494-12a39d637e6f" :step/id #uuid "80da2ac9-41e1-52d3-9494-12a39d637e6f" :step/content "question-2546e8f7-eee4-51d1-b227-0107b1dc1dff" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174299] [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174300] [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174301] [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174303] {:db/id 17592186176034 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" "question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" "question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" "question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175889 :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+7.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=6$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.5x+7 \\\\  & =0.5(6)+7 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" "question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175888 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(82,70).$ So, our actual value is $y=70.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=82$ has the $y$-coordinate $65.$ So, our estimated value is $\\widehat{y}=65.$\n\n![](images/99/99e3741f602802e636e2e49ef755954343079b8c0d98453dac9364ddc08ef16f.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =70-65 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176035 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" "question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" "question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175890 :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c7bf33ee8878c6dc8e33622a5abe79a068b483ed19c0e177ecea31ab34b8777.png)\n\n  \n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=4,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=4$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual} >     \\textrm{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates  this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b02727029ed43c985da639287afa452cbe1985dc2bae8eaa4f16452ac4c01518.png)\n\n   \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/id #uuid "9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/math-academy-id "q-134719" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=-1.5x+2.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=12$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $-14?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =-1.5x+2 \\\\  & =-1.5(12)+2 \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-14-(-16) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" "answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" "answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" "answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/id #uuid "2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/id #uuid "c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/id #uuid "8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/id #uuid "a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/id #uuid "0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176340 :question/problem "An antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $x$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=3.2x+4.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual $5$ decades after the artwork was produced if the actual value of the artwork after $5$ decades is $$23\\,000?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =3.2x+4.5 \\\\  & =3.2(5)+4.5 \\\\  & =20.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =23-20.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,500.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186174298 :answer-field/correct "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" "answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" "answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/id #uuid "844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$(-1\\,500)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/id #uuid "66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$(-2\\,500)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/id #uuid "6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/id #uuid "640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/id #uuid "f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-134737" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.75x+2.25.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=8$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $11.25?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.75x+2.25 \\\\  & =0.75(8)+2.25 \\\\  & =8.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =11.25-8.25 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" "answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" "answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" "answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/id #uuid "91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/id #uuid "fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/id #uuid "0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/id #uuid "a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/id #uuid "5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/id #uuid "66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/math-academy-id "q-134736" :question/problem "A veterinarian collects data on a puppy's height $y$ (in inches) at certain times $x$ (in months) since it was born. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=2.2x+3.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual after $5$ months if the actual height of the $5$-month old puppy is $15.5\\,in?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated height using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.2x+3.5 \\\\  & =2.2(5)+3.5 \\\\  & =14.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =15.5-14.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,in.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/id #uuid "177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" "answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" "answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" "answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/id #uuid "860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.5\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/id #uuid "874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/id #uuid "a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/id #uuid "aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/id #uuid "986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/id #uuid "e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134753" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=1.8x+1.4.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=7$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =1.8x+1.4 \\\\  & =1.8(7)+1.4 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-14 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/id #uuid "790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer-field/choices ["answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" "answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" "answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" "answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" "answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/id #uuid "452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/id #uuid "ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/id #uuid "8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/id #uuid "428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/id #uuid "855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-134788" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f940a05c937b3158ce737959dee4685d216e6d55d6651672aa910cdb2c492f1e.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,1).$ So, our actual value is $y=1.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $0.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=0.$\n\n![](images/93/937c0307a74881c87e6a33c47b32a1ac2d5124326b13538455640cd9fc88c14e.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" "answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" "answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" "answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/id #uuid "a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/id #uuid "fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/id #uuid "27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/id #uuid "e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/id #uuid "6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/id #uuid "fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/math-academy-id "q-134797" :question/problem "![](images/81/815ba0a13bc8cbd7adcfadc63b80d6f2da36c9755166694915fa2f297be27721.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $x$ years after its release to the market. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,12).$ So, our actual value is $y=12.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $10.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=10.$\n\n![](images/ab/ab5e194ac03482b1cee6bdb7aa35e323b40a1ad63769e60acbb000adb7aa1e82.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" "answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" "answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" "answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/id #uuid "a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,000$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/id #uuid "5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,200$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/id #uuid "e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/id #uuid "d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$2\\,000$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/id #uuid "eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176343 :question/problem "![](images/27/278c910d3ce96e613e04cb1b849e57775064c49de45972358c07bfa90d882c8b.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186174316 :answer-field/correct 17592186174317 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/id #uuid "e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134830" :question/problem "![](images/31/31a72edb688af9be0481fc98346aa5655190e32564ddc003eb7bdd1c83d41ee1.png)\n\nAn economist records data on the volume of corn exports $y$ (in thousands of tons) from the United States to a particular country, $x$ number of years since $2010.$\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates (*not* underestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/id #uuid "134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" "answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" "answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" "answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/id #uuid "73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/id #uuid "054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/id #uuid "2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/id #uuid "352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/id #uuid "ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/id #uuid "21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-134825" :question/problem "![](images/57/57ba7828008f3e3c271ae4c1b6d444005f40c09bf6ba99e614f3b6414c1e56c2.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $t$ years after its release to the market. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as time increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/fe18ccc94d0cc98f971b6482d4e31c7ec7066b5cec427108ddd8d1e6609e08ba.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/id #uuid "68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" "answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" "answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" "answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/id #uuid "e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/id #uuid "655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/id #uuid "61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/id #uuid "cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/id #uuid "f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/id #uuid "1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/math-academy-id "q-134824" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae6bc049d3bf3bbdf1a609b6cda4c3b4e9cc1699b387099d265e048a32be68d6.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f5f3a4dc75324a6ef415c987a62139e2dbd51c5b35a56d5a35f410781087c43.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" "answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" "answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" "answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/id #uuid "a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/id #uuid "30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/id #uuid "f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/id #uuid "8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/id #uuid "3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177047 :tutorial/content "Given a dataset of paired numerical observations $(x,y)$ and the corresponding linear regression model $\\widehat{y} =f(x),$ the **residual** for a particular observation $(x, y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-f(x) \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe subtract the *estimated* value predicted by the model from the actual *observed* value.\n\nTo illustrate this concept graphically, consider the following example.\n\nThe owner of an ice cream shop keeps track of the average daily temperature $x$ (measured in $^\\circ \\mathrm{F}$) and the resulting daily ice cream sales $y$ (in dollars). The scatter plot for several randomly selected days and the corresponding linear regression line are shown below. \n\n![](images/fc/fc149b8d911a7a9863df9cc25c635d6155accd676e83e335a65d9083596b779b.png)\n\nSuppose the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny= 2.5 x +165.\n$$\n\nLet's use our regression line to compute the residual of the point with coordinates $\\color{red}(82, 360)$ (shown in red on our graph). \n\nFirst, notice that since the highlighted data point has coordinates ${\\color{red}(82, 360)},$ our actual value is $y = {\\color{red}360}.$\n\nNext, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.5x+165 \\\\  & =2.5(82)+165 \\\\  & =370\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/38/3843c71b50251ae035378507ffb22cfade48dff8e1544d8e1317e4e6d611f7a1.png)\n\nFinally, we compute the residual: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =360-370 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThe residual tells us that the linear model *overestimates* the true volume of ice cream sales by $\\[math]10$ when the outside temperature is $82^\\circ\\,\\textrm{F}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177048 :tutorial/content "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis. \n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line. \n\n![](images/62/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\n    \n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](images/d7/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\n    \n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes: \n\n![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177051 :tutorial/content "![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)\n\nWe should be aware of the following interpretations for residual plots:\n\n- Any point *above* the horizontal axis represents a *positive* residual. A positive residual means that the regression model *underestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\n- Any point *below* the horizontal axis represents a *negative* residual. A negative residual means that the regression model *overestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\nResidual plots can also be used to assess whether a trend line is a \"good\" fit for the corresponding data:\n\n- If a linear trend line is a good fit for the data, the residuals should be scattered randomly above and below the horizontal axis and be relatively close to zero.\n\n- In cases where the residuals show some clear pattern, this usually indicates that the data has no linear trend.\n\nThe residuals are scattered randomly about the horizontal axis in our last example. However, they are not close to zero, indicating that the trend line is a weak fit for the data." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176138 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105808 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-29ae9066-cb5e-58ca-bc97-42812b49b53a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-29ae9066-cb5e-58ca-bc97-42812b49b53a" :question/id #uuid "29ae9066-cb5e-58ca-bc97-42812b49b53a" :question/math-academy-id "q-22657" :question/problem "![](images/6d/6d6009de9ef5df47144f36eb42393b7e9f77ab5c70e3606db09e48bf98289ecb.png)\n\nWhich of the following polygons has the same perimeter as the hexagon $ABCDEF$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The perimeter of the triangle shown below is $17$, as well as the perimeter of the given hexagon. Among the options given, the triangle is the only one that satisfies this. \n\n![](images/e4/e40d126b8304f762f95026016e13c193994fbb7f70f3173a86a35a08526a3bdb.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2b10337-7261-5902-bb66-e43af38982e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2b10337-7261-5902-bb66-e43af38982e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b10337-7261-5902-bb66-e43af38982e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6965421-5124-5c84-acc3-9ace456f77ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-858e9dfa-a8de-51c4-817c-4d66fa093276" "answer-fbd4d47a-0415-50ae-8e04-d71876767c8f" "answer-f2d04142-0375-59e3-8b83-0d47326fe9ce" "answer-a6965421-5124-5c84-acc3-9ace456f77ee" "answer-01b50dcf-3dca-5df9-809e-6982d942ec58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-858e9dfa-a8de-51c4-817c-4d66fa093276" :answer/id #uuid "858e9dfa-a8de-51c4-817c-4d66fa093276" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/00/00bb0e381bc28260b29e35344882c609417b779874659b0fc1b22b18f8b7f36f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbd4d47a-0415-50ae-8e04-d71876767c8f" :answer/id #uuid "fbd4d47a-0415-50ae-8e04-d71876767c8f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/09/091b2911311df4593655b7006bec4bb2c7bc459a3efcbdf5464f953620044a22.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2d04142-0375-59e3-8b83-0d47326fe9ce" :answer/id #uuid "f2d04142-0375-59e3-8b83-0d47326fe9ce" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d7/d7b363e7150899daa28bb3097b6b31174b63beb0f01a9d0b0a6f8382ec5dcafd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6965421-5124-5c84-acc3-9ace456f77ee" :answer/id #uuid "a6965421-5124-5c84-acc3-9ace456f77ee" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/e4/e40d126b8304f762f95026016e13c193994fbb7f70f3173a86a35a08526a3bdb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01b50dcf-3dca-5df9-809e-6982d942ec58" :answer/id #uuid "01b50dcf-3dca-5df9-809e-6982d942ec58" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ee/ee38f7125c6653ef45025cb37edc34859c689afe2989b9152cb71a4438315373.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef8d594b-7df8-58f6-be78-cc667ee70380" "question-9bda3ed0-c16c-5140-97eb-7ad72121a660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef8d594b-7df8-58f6-be78-cc667ee70380" :question/id #uuid "ef8d594b-7df8-58f6-be78-cc667ee70380" :question/math-academy-id "q-67871" :question/problem "In a quadrilateral $ABCD,$ the measures of the sides are $AB=17\\,mm,$ $BC=14\\,mm,$ $CD=2\\,cm,$ and $DA=9\\,mm.$\nWhat is the perimeter of the quadrilateral?" :question/worked-solution "Most of the measures are given in $mm$ (millimeters), so we will start by converting all the measures to $mm$ and adding them up:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =17\\,mm+14\\,mm+\\overset{2\\,cm}{\\overset{⏞}{20\\,mm}}+9\\,mm \\\\  & =60\\,mm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is a large quantity of $\\text{mm},$ we will convert to $\\text{cm}:$\n\n$$\np=60\\,mm=6\\,cm.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac754ef8-8a92-57f1-83bb-568d71efea89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac754ef8-8a92-57f1-83bb-568d71efea89" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac754ef8-8a92-57f1-83bb-568d71efea89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c7ef95ce-2cfe-5f0c-9a38-55d3a654fdd3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e64ef2b-f990-540e-ab94-68e997b2823f" "answer-af42c5cf-a8f0-57e5-9328-b3b57686f2cb" "answer-d59ef339-bd7c-5cf1-8181-b3eea9c355cc" "answer-0b28ace1-d2a4-5cf6-bd0b-d54c77a0ca31" "answer-c7ef95ce-2cfe-5f0c-9a38-55d3a654fdd3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e64ef2b-f990-540e-ab94-68e997b2823f" :answer/id #uuid "7e64ef2b-f990-540e-ab94-68e997b2823f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af42c5cf-a8f0-57e5-9328-b3b57686f2cb" :answer/id #uuid "af42c5cf-a8f0-57e5-9328-b3b57686f2cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d59ef339-bd7c-5cf1-8181-b3eea9c355cc" :answer/id #uuid "d59ef339-bd7c-5cf1-8181-b3eea9c355cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b28ace1-d2a4-5cf6-bd0b-d54c77a0ca31" :answer/id #uuid "0b28ace1-d2a4-5cf6-bd0b-d54c77a0ca31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7ef95ce-2cfe-5f0c-9a38-55d3a654fdd3" :answer/id #uuid "c7ef95ce-2cfe-5f0c-9a38-55d3a654fdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9bda3ed0-c16c-5140-97eb-7ad72121a660" :question/id #uuid "9bda3ed0-c16c-5140-97eb-7ad72121a660" :question/math-academy-id "q-120787" :question/problem "In the regular octagon $ABCDEFGH$, we have $CD=1.5\\,cm.$ What is the perimeter of the octagon?" :question/worked-solution "The perimeter $p$ of a polygon is the sum of the measures of all its sides. Since all the sides of a regular octagon are equal and the measure of one of them is $1.5\\,cm$, we have \n\n$$\np=8\\cdot CD=8\\cdot 1.5=12\\,cm.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9b51d7b-17fc-5ee3-a798-42015df0b697"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9b51d7b-17fc-5ee3-a798-42015df0b697" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b51d7b-17fc-5ee3-a798-42015df0b697" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b01d977b-12e8-59fc-ac22-06c8c441998c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b2e2633-7df5-5313-b16c-b0f4eabf3255" "answer-b01d977b-12e8-59fc-ac22-06c8c441998c" "answer-ba644bff-0fa5-5829-99df-dc9253a8e3ad" "answer-e97ec4f4-b752-5df9-97cf-87185fcd634e" "answer-da6cde5f-8797-5f63-b6e4-8ec5bc065aa6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b2e2633-7df5-5313-b16c-b0f4eabf3255" :answer/id #uuid "0b2e2633-7df5-5313-b16c-b0f4eabf3255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b01d977b-12e8-59fc-ac22-06c8c441998c" :answer/id #uuid "b01d977b-12e8-59fc-ac22-06c8c441998c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba644bff-0fa5-5829-99df-dc9253a8e3ad" :answer/id #uuid "ba644bff-0fa5-5829-99df-dc9253a8e3ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e97ec4f4-b752-5df9-97cf-87185fcd634e" :answer/id #uuid "e97ec4f4-b752-5df9-97cf-87185fcd634e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da6cde5f-8797-5f63-b6e4-8ec5bc065aa6" :answer/id #uuid "da6cde5f-8797-5f63-b6e4-8ec5bc065aa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4303ae32-a6ba-5a31-8a6a-e566692196a7" :activity/id #uuid "4303ae32-a6ba-5a31-8a6a-e566692196a7" :activity/title "The Perimeter of a Polygon" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048921 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-3e2e88f8-0f28-5880-a50b-2393532fb354" "step-2fe99cc3-cf10-59ef-aaff-06e6316d17c8" "step-0c9bd898-fab7-54c1-83ae-93d8a8161ea8"] :activity/first-step "step-3e2e88f8-0f28-5880-a50b-2393532fb354" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3e2e88f8-0f28-5880-a50b-2393532fb354" :step/id #uuid "3e2e88f8-0f28-5880-a50b-2393532fb354" :step/content "question-29ae9066-cb5e-58ca-bc97-42812b49b53a" :step/next "step-2fe99cc3-cf10-59ef-aaff-06e6316d17c8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2fe99cc3-cf10-59ef-aaff-06e6316d17c8" :step/id #uuid "2fe99cc3-cf10-59ef-aaff-06e6316d17c8" :step/content "question-ef8d594b-7df8-58f6-be78-cc667ee70380" :step/next "step-0c9bd898-fab7-54c1-83ae-93d8a8161ea8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0c9bd898-fab7-54c1-83ae-93d8a8161ea8" :step/id #uuid "0c9bd898-fab7-54c1-83ae-93d8a8161ea8" :step/content "question-9bda3ed0-c16c-5140-97eb-7ad72121a660" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124562 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/id #uuid "2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-102805" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation $x{y}^{″}-(x+1){y}^{′}+y=0$ for $x>0.$ Use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x)\\cdot {e}^{x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{x}$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{x}+2{u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({u}^{″}{e}^{x}+2{u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x})-(x+1)({u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x})+u{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+2{u}^{′}x+ux)-{e}^{x}{u}^{′}(x+1)-{e}^{x}u(x+1)+{e}^{x}u & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+2{u}^{′}x+ux-{u}^{′}(x+1)-u(x+1)+u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(2x-x-1)+u(x-x-1+1)) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(x-1)) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}\\ne 0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(x-1)=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}x+w(x-1)=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}x{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}x{e}^{-x}\\,⟹\\,u=-{c}_{1}(1+x){e}^{-x}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{x}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}(-{c}_{1}(1+x){e}^{-x}+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=(1+x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" "answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" "answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" "answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/id #uuid "e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1+x){e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/id #uuid "28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1+{x}^{2}){e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/id #uuid "91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/id #uuid "77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/id #uuid "f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" "question-6cd59b40-dc86-5174-9cba-78e6f66091cf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/id #uuid "6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/math-academy-id "q-86452" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,{e}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-1,{e}^{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\text{ }i-2yz\\text{ }j-{y}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-1,{e}^{2}) & =2{e}^{2}\\text{ }i-2(-1)({e}^{2})\\text{ }j-(-1)^{2}k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{2}\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,{e}^{2})\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" "answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" "answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" "answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/id #uuid "40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},-1,2{e}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/id #uuid "7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/id #uuid "45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/id #uuid "5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/id #uuid "9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124497 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/id #uuid "af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37159" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/id #uuid "79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" "answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" "answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" "answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/id #uuid "9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/id #uuid "8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/id #uuid "21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/id #uuid "f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/id #uuid "c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/id #uuid "39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33453" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,-8,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $2x+y-2z=-7.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=-3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-7 \\\\ 2(1)+(-3)+7 & =2z \\\\ 6 & =2z \\\\ z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,-3,3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-3,3⟩-⟨-2,-8,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+5-8|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,3\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" "answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" "answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" "answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/id #uuid "d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/id #uuid "4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/id #uuid "3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/id #uuid "6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/id #uuid "71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119794 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/id #uuid "39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75094" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-4,{u}_{23}=3,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=-12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" "answer-ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" "answer-70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" "answer-d29b0f99-07ab-51ab-98fe-551c80011b17" "answer-7cf259a9-c7cf-53af-a02f-d46c56183bb5"] :db/ens