ep/next "step-c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" :step/id #uuid "c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" :step/content "question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :step/next "step-d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" :step/id #uuid "d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" :step/content "question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :step/next "step-eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" :step/id #uuid "eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" :step/content 17592186351282 :step/next "step-dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa" :step/id #uuid "dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa" :step/content "question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186118760 :answer-field/choices 17592186118761] [:db/retract 17592186118760 :answer-field/choices 17592186118762] [:db/retract 17592186118760 :answer-field/choices 17592186118763] [:db/retract 17592186118760 :answer-field/choices 17592186118764] [:db/retract 17592186118760 :answer-field/choices 17592186118765] {:db/id 17592186119852 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8be0f924-0f3e-5631-9e67-77a4667752f3" "question-3cd38166-ab43-501c-8a09-bb660de655be" "question-189e5e9d-c4bc-5bb9-8c63-9649351614d1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8be0f924-0f3e-5631-9e67-77a4667752f3" :question/id #uuid "8be0f924-0f3e-5631-9e67-77a4667752f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-43109" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-8y+3z=2 \\\\ 6y-3z=-7 \\\\ x-5y+4z=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+(-8)y+3z=2 \\\\ 0x+6y+(-3)z=-7 \\\\ 1x+(-5)y+4z=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5a66b44b-6b9e-5088-92dd-3e1f0889e8b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a66b44b-6b9e-5088-92dd-3e1f0889e8b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a66b44b-6b9e-5088-92dd-3e1f0889e8b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-22f9ed04-9d1d-5af3-b8ea-58280ed15c9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-889308d6-5850-58f0-9c91-23f4fd38db14" "answer-02901c74-dd5e-55a8-a30e-d37d23988f6c" "answer-f6e0ff00-c772-536b-a3bd-7591ea83a72f" "answer-d73ce50d-5dd1-5828-9bcd-7fd2823a2ef5" "answer-22f9ed04-9d1d-5af3-b8ea-58280ed15c9f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-889308d6-5850-58f0-9c91-23f4fd38db14" :answer/id #uuid "889308d6-5850-58f0-9c91-23f4fd38db14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -10 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02901c74-dd5e-55a8-a30e-d37d23988f6c" :answer/id #uuid "02901c74-dd5e-55a8-a30e-d37d23988f6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -10\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6e0ff00-c772-536b-a3bd-7591ea83a72f" :answer/id #uuid "f6e0ff00-c772-536b-a3bd-7591ea83a72f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d73ce50d-5dd1-5828-9bcd-7fd2823a2ef5" :answer/id #uuid "d73ce50d-5dd1-5828-9bcd-7fd2823a2ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22f9ed04-9d1d-5af3-b8ea-58280ed15c9f" :answer/id #uuid "22f9ed04-9d1d-5af3-b8ea-58280ed15c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3cd38166-ab43-501c-8a09-bb660de655be" :question/id #uuid "3cd38166-ab43-501c-8a09-bb660de655be" :question/math-academy-id "q-43120" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-8y+5z=8 \\\\ -4x-6y+3z=-1 \\\\ x-4z=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{z}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(-2)x+(-8)y+5z=8 \\\\ (-4)x+(-6)y+3z=-1 \\\\ 1x+0y+(-4)z=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1dde4f08-b0b2-5881-b757-0ce139acae19"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1dde4f08-b0b2-5881-b757-0ce139acae19" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dde4f08-b0b2-5881-b757-0ce139acae19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0612e921-5057-58c7-8bb3-0c5741bb3803" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0359c967-a736-556a-aa0f-b1dd2a3da13c" "answer-7c92dc9c-1ea6-5198-b638-55d04bb60a37" "answer-0612e921-5057-58c7-8bb3-0c5741bb3803" "answer-65de8e7a-c592-535e-8398-2751781df9fa" "answer-11916100-9121-5d1e-a1ef-24a6f295f8fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0359c967-a736-556a-aa0f-b1dd2a3da13c" :answer/id #uuid "0359c967-a736-556a-aa0f-b1dd2a3da13c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c92dc9c-1ea6-5198-b638-55d04bb60a37" :answer/id #uuid "7c92dc9c-1ea6-5198-b638-55d04bb60a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0612e921-5057-58c7-8bb3-0c5741bb3803" :answer/id #uuid "0612e921-5057-58c7-8bb3-0c5741bb3803" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65de8e7a-c592-535e-8398-2751781df9fa" :answer/id #uuid "65de8e7a-c592-535e-8398-2751781df9fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11916100-9121-5d1e-a1ef-24a6f295f8fc" :answer/id #uuid "11916100-9121-5d1e-a1ef-24a6f295f8fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}8 & -8 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120441 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z=4 \\\\ y-4z=-6 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}1x+(-3)y+1z=4 \\\\ 0x+1y+(-4)z=-6 \\\\ 3x+1y+1z=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118760 :answer-field/correct "answer-8711aafc-d2ac-5f68-a103-0f5c1e832744" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6d537ef-517e-5954-9a01-2bc13b06765d" "answer-e8f75c46-d176-5685-bdd6-4de61fe2da21" "answer-fef7040b-92b0-52c5-a4ae-d7caae6a89de" "answer-8711aafc-d2ac-5f68-a103-0f5c1e832744" "answer-02b9a8c6-b9bd-5899-bd09-098131be7790"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6d537ef-517e-5954-9a01-2bc13b06765d" :answer/id #uuid "a6d537ef-517e-5954-9a01-2bc13b06765d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8f75c46-d176-5685-bdd6-4de61fe2da21" :answer/id #uuid "e8f75c46-d176-5685-bdd6-4de61fe2da21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fef7040b-92b0-52c5-a4ae-d7caae6a89de" :answer/id #uuid "fef7040b-92b0-52c5-a4ae-d7caae6a89de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8711aafc-d2ac-5f68-a103-0f5c1e832744" :answer/id #uuid "8711aafc-d2ac-5f68-a103-0f5c1e832744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02b9a8c6-b9bd-5899-bd09-098131be7790" :answer/id #uuid "02b9a8c6-b9bd-5899-bd09-098131be7790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-189e5e9d-c4bc-5bb9-8c63-9649351614d1" :question/id #uuid "189e5e9d-c4bc-5bb9-8c63-9649351614d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42694" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-9y+4z=1 \\\\ 3x-2y-5z=7 \\\\ 3x-8y+2z=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{z}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+(-9)y+4z=1 \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+(-5)z=7 \\\\ 3x+(-8)y+2z=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7fed87a8-5cdb-5f1a-a7fe-3143ef0b136a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7fed87a8-5cdb-5f1a-a7fe-3143ef0b136a" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fed87a8-5cdb-5f1a-a7fe-3143ef0b136a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3cbe2bb6-b29c-57e7-b971-65b7aab22fe4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72034927-2307-593c-b051-e44ef8090945" "answer-3cbe2bb6-b29c-57e7-b971-65b7aab22fe4" "answer-917db11c-9f99-581d-9128-f4df28c7132c" "answer-850388e7-886b-5c54-95f5-aa6b5e305a57" "answer-22a2de46-ad88-5316-8e73-b1ff7775cc80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72034927-2307-593c-b051-e44ef8090945" :answer/id #uuid "72034927-2307-593c-b051-e44ef8090945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cbe2bb6-b29c-57e7-b971-65b7aab22fe4" :answer/id #uuid "3cbe2bb6-b29c-57e7-b971-65b7aab22fe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-917db11c-9f99-581d-9128-f4df28c7132c" :answer/id #uuid "917db11c-9f99-581d-9128-f4df28c7132c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-850388e7-886b-5c54-95f5-aa6b5e305a57" :answer/id #uuid "850388e7-886b-5c54-95f5-aa6b5e305a57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22a2de46-ad88-5316-8e73-b1ff7775cc80" :answer/id #uuid "22a2de46-ad88-5316-8e73-b1ff7775cc80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119789 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-42ee0be6-4308-53bc-b367-0e542cac978e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-42ee0be6-4308-53bc-b367-0e542cac978e" :question/id #uuid "42ee0be6-4308-53bc-b367-0e542cac978e" :question/math-academy-id "q-43121" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z=1 \\\\ 6x-2y-z=-14 \\\\ 3x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $27,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+1z=1 \\\\ 6x+(-2)y+(-1)z=-14 \\\\ 3x+1y+(-1)z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -14 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -14 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -14 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-2+14)-3(6+42)+(6+6) \\\\  & =24-144+12 \\\\  & =-108.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{-108}{27}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b8fd5cb6-f113-5503-be05-ca917de23415"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b8fd5cb6-f113-5503-be05-ca917de23415" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8fd5cb6-f113-5503-be05-ca917de23415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2bec32dd-29a6-5607-920d-c35b9a232d65" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7bf56a6c-9b35-56b5-83b1-eab01b39b95f" "answer-2bec32dd-29a6-5607-920d-c35b9a232d65" "answer-c4ae4810-f1e6-544a-a09e-ed9a32b9bd9a" "answer-131b8e36-82f8-5b9c-9ba5-e64dead4cde3" "answer-d88503a5-902e-5a41-ab49-65ce7f2c3952"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bf56a6c-9b35-56b5-83b1-eab01b39b95f" :answer/id #uuid "7bf56a6c-9b35-56b5-83b1-eab01b39b95f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bec32dd-29a6-5607-920d-c35b9a232d65" :answer/id #uuid "2bec32dd-29a6-5607-920d-c35b9a232d65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ae4810-f1e6-544a-a09e-ed9a32b9bd9a" :answer/id #uuid "c4ae4810-f1e6-544a-a09e-ed9a32b9bd9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-131b8e36-82f8-5b9c-9ba5-e64dead4cde3" :answer/id #uuid "131b8e36-82f8-5b9c-9ba5-e64dead4cde3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d88503a5-902e-5a41-ab49-65ce7f2c3952" :answer/id #uuid "d88503a5-902e-5a41-ab49-65ce7f2c3952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119791 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8259ae37-435b-52c3-a2f0-cf085e62a133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8259ae37-435b-52c3-a2f0-cf085e62a133" :question/id #uuid "8259ae37-435b-52c3-a2f0-cf085e62a133" :question/math-academy-id "q-42682" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}kx+2y-4z=-4 \\\\ x-2y+5z=-6 \\\\ 10x+y+2z=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $x=-\\frac{20}{3}$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $12-9k,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=12-9k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4(-4-5)-2(-12-40)-4(-6+16) \\\\  & =36+104-40 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{100}{12-9k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=-\\frac{20}{3}.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{100}{12-9k} & =-\\frac{20}{3} \\\\ 15 & =-12+9k \\\\ 9k & =27 \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9df02a6a-4e09-5087-b781-68996219ec42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9df02a6a-4e09-5087-b781-68996219ec42" :answer-field/id #uuid "9df02a6a-4e09-5087-b781-68996219ec42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b477092-14a5-585d-a218-bfd1bf2d5620" :answer-field/choices ["answer-381978cd-5ab7-51e7-b541-211370f63648" "answer-a549f739-e810-54df-a9ab-4502b087167f" "answer-fec613a5-e3db-55c6-8737-642a2ed8c695" "answer-0b477092-14a5-585d-a218-bfd1bf2d5620" "answer-f21927cf-9af8-5e15-9789-74ae85afddc3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-381978cd-5ab7-51e7-b541-211370f63648" :answer/id #uuid "381978cd-5ab7-51e7-b541-211370f63648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a549f739-e810-54df-a9ab-4502b087167f" :answer/id #uuid "a549f739-e810-54df-a9ab-4502b087167f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fec613a5-e3db-55c6-8737-642a2ed8c695" :answer/id #uuid "fec613a5-e3db-55c6-8737-642a2ed8c695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b477092-14a5-585d-a218-bfd1bf2d5620" :answer/id #uuid "0b477092-14a5-585d-a218-bfd1bf2d5620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f21927cf-9af8-5e15-9789-74ae85afddc3" :answer/id #uuid "f21927cf-9af8-5e15-9789-74ae85afddc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121026 :tutorial/content "Cramer's rule applies to square systems of linear equations with any number of variables. In this lesson, we will practice applying Cramer's rule to solve $3 \\times 3$ systems of equations.\n\nSuppose we have a square system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y+{a}_{13}z={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y+{a}_{23}z={b}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{31}x+{a}_{32}y+{a}_{33}z={b}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ![](images/39/39c4a39573975acc249a4402799f40ef8d72666d4da03d6c4ed6cc299bc7fc52.svg). \nThen Cramer's rule states that\n\n$$\n\\left< x,y,z \\right> = \\left\\langle  \\dfrac{D_x}{D}, \\dfrac{D_y}{D}, \\dfrac{D_z}{D} \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nis the unique solution of the system, where\n\n![](images/dc/dcda1374b4582e7978133bbf3cea0375b40095d353573f826a3bac7f212dfc03.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121047 :tutorial/content "To demonstrate using Cramer's rule on a $3 \\times 3$ system, consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y+z=9 \\\\ 2y+3z=7 \\\\ -8x+y+6z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y+1z=9 \\\\ 0x+2y+3z=7 \\\\ -8x+1y+6z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start finding the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 6\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(12-3)-2(0+24)+(0+16) \\\\  & =36-48+16 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $D_x,$ $D_y,$ and $D_z.$\n\n- To find $D_x,$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the *first* column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & =9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9(12-3)-2(42-0)+(7-0) \\\\  & =81-84+7 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find $D_y,$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the *second* column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 6\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(42)-9(0+24)+(0+56) \\\\  & =168-216+56 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find $D_z,$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the *third* column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}|+9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-7)-2(0+56)+9(0+16) \\\\  & =-28-112+144 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the system is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩ & =⟨\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{4},\\frac{8}{4},\\frac{4}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119998 :activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-80dffb9b-6686-5250-93b4-d26b471b47b4" :activity/id #uuid "80dffb9b-6686-5250-93b4-d26b471b47b4" :activity/title "Global vs. Local Extrema and Critical Points of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049676 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-90845892-a21e-5ed0-8f4d-4176220e88dd" "step-e73ff290-95f1-54f7-9f82-02df0d72039f" "step-ab83c715-96e6-5979-ad33-c4a45c733837" "step-7aed301f-ecb7-5892-aaed-84080d4f66c0" "step-0e56b147-81e4-5b76-ba78-f42888fc798d"] :activity/first-step "step-90845892-a21e-5ed0-8f4d-4176220e88dd" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-90845892-a21e-5ed0-8f4d-4176220e88dd" :step/id #uuid "90845892-a21e-5ed0-8f4d-4176220e88dd" :ste