g gives the graph of $y=f(-x)+2?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(-x)+2,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(-x).$\n\n![](images/1b/1b60eeb882c85423bb0550c2b6def0d073d53747479bf322976db313ffdf4109.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, translate the result  up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=f(-x)+2.$\n\n![](images/58/58a681bf9aa47521b30761e904dad8e816e2077387c28b132d2480bb39ea4baa.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2dd6fd98-c961-563c-bc24-20e9ae8af96f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2dd6fd98-c961-563c-bc24-20e9ae8af96f" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd6fd98-c961-563c-bc24-20e9ae8af96f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6fad0e56-8403-5347-b45c-ba6f872ed247" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fad0e56-8403-5347-b45c-ba6f872ed247" "answer-a930a6e8-3abd-543f-8c9a-8505f9229673" "answer-893b058d-9aef-5c0a-915b-3bd06e89338b" "answer-3a17fc34-f3a5-52e2-abe9-26bde3624def" "answer-18e3e3c2-5496-53cf-8c02-e876d2a94f5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fad0e56-8403-5347-b45c-ba6f872ed247" :answer/id #uuid "6fad0e56-8403-5347-b45c-ba6f872ed247" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/0f/0f8dace29f2d5764ca43b58946405d1b406e9898facce07ca1089c02b798e246.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a930a6e8-3abd-543f-8c9a-8505f9229673" :answer/id #uuid "a930a6e8-3abd-543f-8c9a-8505f9229