db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0c2f224c-fc34-5e4b-af33-9729624ea81e" :step/id #uuid "0c2f224c-fc34-5e4b-af33-9729624ea81e" :step/content "question-41a5c3bd-58e0-5924-89f4-127ab078d31e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157291 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b53fe7a0-ceb1-5bb0-aa72-c767bfb8907a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157095 :question/problem "![](images/dc/dcddc9ee6fe49965ea4f261fcb43c6f7ccd14193910e864b950745ef513e67a6.png)\n\nThe sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ are shown in the Venn diagram above. Find $X\\cup Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The union $X \\cup Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $X$ or $Y,$ or both. To represent $X \\cup Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained within either $X$ or $Y,$ or both.\n\n![](images/c9/c94cfc38872dfe0673e112e09feec7781ab4f247f08932d1d8ecd167b4a99d32.png)\n\nThe elements $1,2,3,4,5,8$ are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. Therefore, the union of $X$ and $Y$ is\n\n$$\nX \\cup Y = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,8 \\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157280 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3ece29a0-cc0f-5be6-9001-b8cc96566290" "question-e3ebe755-cc28-56a9-a6f9-b3ea716cdfc2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157084 :question/problem "Given the sets $X = \\{2, 5, 7, 8\\},$ $Y = \\{1, 3, 5\\},$ and $Z = \\{2, 4, 6, 8\\},$ find $X \\cup Y,$ $Y \\cup Z,$ and $Z \\cup X.$" :question/worked-solution "The union $X \\cup Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{2,5,7,8\\}\\cup \\{1,3,5\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,5,7,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe union $Y \\cup Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $Y$ or $Z,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y\\cup Z & =\\{1,3,5\\}\\cup \\{2,4,6,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe union $Z \\cup X$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $Z$ or $X,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z\\cup X & =\\{2,4,6,8\\}\\cup \\{2,5,7,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,5,6,7,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157281 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b7be71bb-2a94-5959-b6e1-bd279930afab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157085 :question/problem "Let $A$ and $B$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $A \\cup B?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\cup B$ is the *union* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…\\}\\cup \\{6,12,18,24,30,36,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,6,8,12,16,18,20,24,28,30,32,36,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233058 :question/problem "![](images/1f/1f3d0b514bc4ec701b6ac755b82cec7246a7a819400108e1733759eb0a2fec86.png)\n\nGiven the sets $A=\\{o,p,q,r\\}$ and $B=\\{q,r,v,w\\},$ find $A\\cup B.$" :question/worked-solution "The union $A\\cup B$ consists of all the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both. To represent $A\\cup B,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\n![](images/79/7984b0cb81df816388aa0d5cbf860fc4bdad9f7e871e8671d4616ded02bcaf5b.png)\n\nThe elements $o,p,q,r,v,w$ are in either $A$ or $B$, or both. Therefore, the union of $A$ and $B$ is\n\n$$\nA\\cup B=\\{o,p,q,r,v,w\\}.\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a8d0de6-4a95-55f5-a7ec-01b6ea620608"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a8d0de6-4a95-55f5-a7ec-01b6ea620608" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a8d0de6-4a95-55f5-a7ec-01b6ea620608" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-db8fd15c-4018-59c8-93f1-bbad4a93602d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1959e253-4fde-51cc-90d9-1cc12992f1d8" "answer-db8fd15c-4018-59c8-93f1-bbad4a93602d" "answer-91314f35-99d9-59e4-8b56-599e104f792a" "answer-69a8a399-3c2b-5b9a-8063-1886a09b305f" "answer-473909b9-0dad-56ec-abe7-7c8bf49c7ca5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1959e253-4fde-51cc-90d9-1cc12992f1d8" :answer/id #uuid "1959e253-4fde-51cc-90d9-1cc12992f1d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{o,p,q,r,v,w,x\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db8fd15c-4018-59c8-93f1-bbad4a93602d" :answer/id #uuid "db8fd15c-4018-59c8-93f1-bbad4a93602d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{o,p,q,r,v,w\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91314f35-99d9-59e4-8b56-599e104f792a" :answer/id #uuid "91314f35-99d9-59e4-8b56-599e104f792a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{o,p,v,w\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69a8a399-3c2b-5b9a-8063-1886a09b305f" :answer/id #uuid "69a8a399-3c2b-5b9a-8063-1886a09b305f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{q,r\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-473909b9-0dad-56ec-abe7-7c8bf49c7ca5" :answer/id #uuid "473909b9-0dad-56ec-abe7-7c8bf49c7ca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{v,w,x\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b53fe7a0-ceb1-5bb0-aa72-c767bfb8907a" :question/id #uuid "b53fe7a0-ceb1-5bb0-aa72-c767bfb8907a" :question/math-academy-id "q-101943" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e27737b6aac8caa70549393b78c11ea3d6cc97cb54ec51b557744dfc456359d0.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S=\\{7,9\\}$ and $T=\\{10,25,50\\},$ find $S\\cup T.$" :question/worked-solution "The union $S\\cup T$ consists of all the elements that are in either $S$ or $T,$ or both. To represent $S\\cup T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in either $S$ or $T,$ or both.\n\n![](images/34/34587d9fc3201b9251d233a813d96ed355b8285e64dd1b7d71c72f91c8ee5efb.png)\n\nThe elements $7,9,10,25,50$ are in either $S$ or $T.$ Therefore, the union of $S$ and $T$ is\n\n$$\nS\\cup T=\\{7,9,10,25,50\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-679567f8-dae9-5539-b613-8e9383f63984"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-679567f8-dae9-5539-b613-8e9383f63984" :answer-field/id #uuid "679567f8-dae9-5539-b613-8e9383f63984" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9cefa41e-4772-5d52-b9f8-088d0b86cba8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d330b4e0-24a7-5b5b-8a77-e6459a08ea1f" "answer-0cbb00e8-fa3a-5a23-a8f1-0bae0667c2ff" "answer-2f08521a-3060-562d-954a-c40b0f5aa7e7" "answer-9cefa41e-4772-5d52-b9f8-088d0b86cba8" "answer-4194f29b-c0cd-5734-a67d-babe2dbcf1a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d330b4e0-24a7-5b5b-8a77-e6459a08ea1f" :answer/id #uuid "d330b4e0-24a7-5b5b-8a77-e6459a08ea1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{10\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cbb00e8-fa3a-5a23-a8f1-0bae0667c2ff" :answer/id #uuid "0cbb00e8-fa3a-5a23-a8f1-0bae0667c2ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{7,25,50\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f08521a-3060-562d-954a-c40b0f5aa7e7" :answer/id #uuid "2f08521a-3060-562d-954a-c40b0f5aa7e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{7,25\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cefa41e-4772-5d52-b9f8-088d0b86cba8" :answer/id #uuid "9cefa41e-4772-5d52-b9f8-088d0b86cba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{7,9,10,25,50\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4194f29b-c0cd-5734-a67d-babe2dbcf1a9" :answer/id #uuid "4194f29b-c0cd-5734-a67d-babe2dbcf1a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ece29a0-cc0f-5